--TEST--
`Core\IO::readBytes` of a file outside the directories `fs.read` grants throws `RuntimeError` naming the capability, even when the file exists
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\IO::readBytes
echo Core\IO::readBytes("public/inside.txt") as string;

try {
    Core\IO::readBytes("private/outside.txt");
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $denied) {
    echo $denied->message, "\n";
}
--FILE public/inside.txt--
inside
--FILE private/outside.txt--
outside
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["public"]
--EXPECTF--
inside
Core\IO::readBytes needs the capability `fs.read` for %s%eprivate%eoutside.txt, which is not granted
help: add `read = ["%s"]` under `[capabilities.fs]` in nvs.toml
